# Keep the shipped sources byte-for-byte identical on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone (git's default `core.autocrlf=true`) rewrites
# every LF in these files to CRLF. Nothing here breaks at runtime — the bundles
# are plain JS — but it makes `git diff` noisy for contributors and, more
# importantly, means a checksum of the installed `lib/client.js` no longer
# matches the one published here. The plugin ships ONE artifact that every
# platform must consume unmodified, so the line endings are pinned at the
# repository boundary instead of left to each machine's git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched, never diffed.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.tgz binary

# Generated test captures and logs are not part of the package.
*.log -text
